1
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:06,817
YAMU, YAMU, YAMU,

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:08,177
YAMU, YAMU,

3
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:09,120
YAMU,

4
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:16,220
YAMU!

5
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:31,620
Your moves!

6
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:09,517
Give me seconds of that cheese.

7
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:10,659
Yeah, and the ham.

8
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:13,393
And that weird jelly cake-looking thing.

9
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:17,160
If this was a dual munchers
competition, you two would win.

10
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:18,420
On behalf of Mr.

11
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:19,697
Maximilian Pegasus,

12
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:22,577
I'd like to congratulate the
four finalists and welcome

13
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:25,997
them to this final phase of the
Duelist Kingdom competition.

14
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:29,480
I trust you all have your
playoff entry cards. Huh?

15
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:34,157
In your invitation to the Duelist
Kingdom, you received these two cards.

16
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:37,517
Glory of the King's Hand and
Glory of the King's Opposite Hand.

17
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:40,837
You must have one of these to
participate in the final tournament.

18
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:43,037
Those without them are disqualified.

19
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,657
So that's what they're for.

20
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:46,681
Each card provides unique prizes.

21
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:50,957
The Glory of the King's Hand card is
needed to claim the $3 million cash prize.

22
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:55,137
The Opposite Hand card allows the winner
to challenge Pegasus for the championship.

23
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:56,420
Now he tells me.

24
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:57,397
I don't have either one.

25
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:01,680
Of the millions of cards I own, I
run across the two that I don't.

26
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:03,360
I have to get me one.

27
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,657
To make tomorrow's tournament interesting,

28
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:08,916
your host has added a special
ingredient to your soup.

29
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:12,940
It's staring at me.

30
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:15,160
Hey, mine's eyeball free.

31
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:18,704
Hey, this is worse than
having a fly in my soup.

32
00:02:19,140 --> 00:02:21,980
Open up the eye and look
inside it, if you will.

33
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:25,424
Each of you has been
randomly assigned a letter.

34
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,840
Oh, what's this for?

35
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:31,530
Hmm?

36
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:32,470
Hmm.

37
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:35,777
And now the island's
computer will pair up the

38
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:38,625
letters to determine
tomorrow's duel match-ups.

39
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:41,446
Gee, I wonder who's going
to have to face who.

40
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:42,530
Good.

41
00:02:42,613 --> 00:02:45,557
Once I know who I'm dueling,
I can use tonight to prepare.

42
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:50,169
It doesn't matter who I'm up against if
I don't have one of them glory cards.

43
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:53,240
And tomorrow's duels are as follows.

44
00:02:53,720 --> 00:02:56,660
A versus B, C versus D.

45
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,260
Who has C?

46
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,140
Me, runt.

47
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:03,417
All right, it's payback for
trapping us in that cave.

48
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:06,735
Once I crush you, you wish
you were still in that cave.

49
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,282
Looks like it's you and me, Mai.

50
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:11,480
I'm looking forward to this duel.

51
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:14,460
Yeah, me too, and may
the best duelist win.

52
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:17,400
The duels are set.

53
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:22,379
Yugi Moto versus Mai Valentine, and
Bandit Keith versus Joey Wheeler.

54
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:24,397
Please enjoy the rest of this feast,

55
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:28,774
because for three of you tomorrow,
Your long journey will end in failure.

56
00:03:33,680 --> 00:03:35,240
So it has begun.

57
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:45,800
I'm stuffed like a sumo wrestler.

58
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,760
Oh, that was good.

59
00:03:48,180 --> 00:03:51,121
I can't believe you drank
the entire eyeball soup.

60
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:52,240
Hey there, Joey.

61
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:53,790
Huh?

62
00:03:53,873 --> 00:03:54,703
We better get to bed.

63
00:03:54,786 --> 00:03:55,857
We'll need our rest if we're all going to

64
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:58,528
be in top shape for the
tournament tomorrow.

65
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:01,213
Youg, what's the point?

66
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:03,380
Since I don't have that card, huh?

67
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:07,537
Actually, this Glory of King's
hand card is yours, Joey.

68
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:11,149
Why don't you just think of it
as an early birthday present?

69
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:12,070
Yugi!

70
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:14,020
But Youg, you need it.

71
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:19,167
The rules never said we needed both cards
to compete, so we each only need one.

72
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,150
Yeah.

73
00:04:21,233 --> 00:04:23,840
If you give up now, who's
going to save your sister?

74
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:28,557
What kind of big brother would you be if
you didn't even try to win the prize money?

75
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:29,470
Yugi?

76
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:32,420
And besides, Joey, think about the odds.

77
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:36,597
If we're both in the tournament, it doubles
our chances of winning the entire thing.

78
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:37,720
So take it, okay?

79
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:39,110
Take it.

80
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:40,810
Okay.

81
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:42,712
You're a real pal, Yugi.

82
00:04:44,380 --> 00:04:47,400
All this lovey-dovey stuff
is making my skin crawl.

83
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:51,469
So good night, boys and girls,
and catch you tomorrow, Yugi.

84
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:54,474
Good night, everybody.

85
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:56,077
Tomorrow's a big day.

86
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:56,990
Good night.

87
00:04:57,073 --> 00:04:57,903
Later.

88
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:00,460
Night, guys. Yugi. Huh?

89
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:03,793
Listen, thanks again for bailing me out.

90
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:05,115
You're the best, pal.

91
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,597
Well, time to catch some Zs.

92
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:09,940
Don't snore too loud.

93
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:11,060
I don't snore.

94
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:14,731
You kept us up half the night
at the campfire, right, Yugi?

95
00:05:14,980 --> 00:05:15,810
Uh...

96
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:23,000
Well, Grandpa, I've made it this far.

97
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:25,717
A couple of more victories
and we'll go home.

98
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:26,630
Together.

99
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:32,740
Okay, I'll have to fine-tune
my deck if I'm to beat Yugi.

100
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:35,640
Even if it takes me all night.

101
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,337
Bavarian cream hit this spot right now.

102
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:40,800
Glazes and crawlers and...

103
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,680
Gigantic donut!

104
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,765
The one night I get to sleep in
a decent bed and I'm wide awake.

105
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:52,760
Huh? Who is it?

106
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:55,980
Oh, what's up, guys?

107
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:57,140
Trouble, Thea.

108
00:05:57,340 --> 00:06:00,057
Tristan thinks that Pegasus
cheats in all his duels.

109
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:00,970
Well, he does.

110
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:03,460
Hmm. No.

111
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,877
You really think he beat Kaiba
this morning by cheating?

112
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,240
Yeah. I mean,

113
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,357
Kaiba's one of the world's top duelists,

114
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:12,717
but Pegasus beat him
like he was an amateur.

115
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,630
That's true.

116
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:16,520
No one can beat Kaiba that easily.

117
00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:18,916
At least not playing fair and square.

118
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,157
The way he was dueling,

119
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:23,577
it seemed like he knew what cards
were in Kaiba's hand the entire time.

120
00:06:23,660 --> 00:06:25,137
I'm telling you the truth.

121
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:27,540
Pegasus is as bogus as a $3 bill.

122
00:06:27,860 --> 00:06:28,720
He's a punk.

123
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:30,437
You can't trust that guy.

124
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:34,049
Even if you're right about
Pegasus, what can we do, Tristan?

125
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:34,990
Plenty.

126
00:06:35,073 --> 00:06:36,877
We'll find out how Pegasus cheated.

127
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:40,017
There has to be some clue
down at the dueling platform.

128
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:42,757
We'll expose Pegasus for
the fraud that he is.

129
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:46,722
With all the gods everywhere, we'll
need help from Yu-Gi and Joey.

130
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:48,917
No, they have to rest for the tournament.

131
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,357
And besides, a herd of
elephants won't wake Joey.

132
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:52,400
It's up to us.

133
00:06:52,600 --> 00:06:55,740
We have to do this all by
ourselves. I'm with you.

134
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:08,600
Grandpa, is that you?

135
00:07:09,940 --> 00:07:12,757
Yu-Gi, I must speak with you.

136
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:15,200
Grandpa, where are you?

137
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:17,860
Follow my voice.

138
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:25,340
Keep searching, guys.

139
00:07:25,740 --> 00:07:27,977
There has to be a hidden
camera or something.

140
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:29,825
Maybe Pegasus isn't a cheater.

141
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,706
He could be good at guessing
cards like a psychic or something.

142
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:35,940
I once spoke to a psychic.

143
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:38,997
The lady said I'll have a nice
girlfriend within six months.

144
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:41,400
It's been a year, not a single date.

145
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:43,720
I don't believe in psychic powers.

146
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:48,350
Huh?

147
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:50,660
What's wrong, Taya? Look!

148
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:52,520
Tristan, you're back!

149
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:54,220
Something on my back?

150
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:58,150
Huh?

151
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:00,860
Isn't that strange?

152
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:03,240
How can Moonlight enter this room?

153
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:04,910
Tristan,

154
00:08:04,993 --> 00:08:07,397
go stand on the dueling
platform and pretend

155
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:09,877
to hold a card up just
like you're dueling.

156
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:10,790
Sure.

157
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:20,440
What do you see?

158
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:23,409
There's a tower right
across the courtyard.

159
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:27,537
And isn't it convenient that the
window faces in this exact direction?

160
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:30,857
It'd be a piece of cake for
one of Pegasus' goons to hide

161
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:33,977
in the tower with a telescope
and spy on Kaiba's hand.

162
00:08:34,060 --> 00:08:37,060
Then the goon relays Kaiba's cards.

163
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:40,361
Pegasus could be hiding a
receiver under his hair.

164
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,312
Good thinking, Sherlock.

165
00:08:42,420 --> 00:08:45,077
There's bound to be tons of
proof hidden in that tower.

166
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:46,984
Let's get over there right now.

167
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,620
What about the gods?

168
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:52,220
You'll be safe with me.

169
00:08:52,820 --> 00:08:53,650
Grandpa!

170
00:08:53,733 --> 00:08:56,060
Yogi, beware of Pegasus.

171
00:08:56,940 --> 00:09:02,380
You must stop him or he could
destroy the entire world. Pegasus?

172
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:04,980
I'm coming, Grandpa!

173
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:14,080
Oh, this castle's like a maze.

174
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:15,457
Shh, keep it down.

175
00:09:15,540 --> 00:09:16,737
There's goons around that corner.

176
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:18,097
There's goons around every corner.

177
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:19,560
I said, shh, this way.

178
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:21,762
We're running around in circles.

179
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:24,508
It'll be daytime before
we get to the tower.

180
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:27,080
Hey, look at what I found.

181
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:29,420
What's that for?

182
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:32,180
This grappling hook gives me a great idea.

183
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:34,840
Harpy Lady combined with Cyber Shield.

184
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:39,994
Yugi's already familiar with this
combo because he saw my duel with Joey.

185
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,860
He knows my deck almost as well as I do.

186
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:50,907
If I'm to beat him, I can't rely
on my same old bag of tricks.

187
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:58,040
Well, time to snatch me
one of those special cards.

188
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:02,890
Grandpa!

189
00:10:02,973 --> 00:10:03,803
Where are you?

190
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:04,960
I can't find you!

191
00:10:06,940 --> 00:10:07,770
You!

192
00:10:07,853 --> 00:10:09,560
Beware of Pegasus!

193
00:10:11,180 --> 00:10:14,320
Pegasus wields shadow powers
of incredible strength,

194
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:17,306
much stronger than anyone
could have imagined!

195
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:18,710
But how?

196
00:10:18,793 --> 00:10:19,995
How is that possible?

197
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:44,160
I can't believe your plan is to enter
the tower from the outside. Yep.

198
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:47,297
You wanted to avoid all the guards.

199
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:48,897
I don't see goons up here.

200
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:53,274
Grandpa, tell me how can Pegasus'
shadow magic still be growing in power?

201
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:57,146
Every soul he traps in the shadow
realm increases his strength.

202
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:58,830
Ah!

203
00:10:58,913 --> 00:10:59,743
He's got to be stopped!

204
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:10,220
No! Kaiba! Grandpa!

205
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:13,170
Mokuba!

206
00:11:13,253 --> 00:11:14,200
This is wrong!

207
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:15,500
This is terrible!

208
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,720
Save me, Yugi!

209
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:20,120
Save me, Yugi!

210
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:30,137
All right, Taya, take the
lead and we'll follow you.

211
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:34,417
That way, in case you lose your grip
and fall off, one of us can catch you.

212
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:35,800
You're next, Yugi.

213
00:11:36,180 --> 00:11:37,680
He wants you, Yugi!

214
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:40,640
Why is Pegasus after me?

215
00:11:41,140 --> 00:11:44,837
Pegasus unlocked tremendous magic
with his single Millennium Item.

216
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:48,685
How much power do you think he
will wield if he has your puzzle?

217
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:55,422
Tristan, that's not the
rope, that's my leg Well,

218
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:59,040
climb faster Grandpa,
how can I stop Pegasus?

219
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:03,097
Just as Pegasus learned to harness
the magic of his Millennium Eye

220
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:07,280
You must also learn to control the
power of your own Millennium Item

221
00:12:07,940 --> 00:12:08,940
My puzzle?

222
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:12,600
Yes, Yuki, your Millennium Puzzle But how?

223
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:16,760
That you must discover on
your own Whatever it takes,

224
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:19,980
Pegasus must be defeated If he wins,

225
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:23,477
with his unlimited shadow powers
And the magic of the Millennium

226
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:28,960
Items He can unleash Armageddon
upon the entire world Hulk! Grandpa!

227
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:30,780
You can do this, Yogi!

228
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:32,800
I believe in you!

229
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:37,660
We're in

230
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:45,000
Your plans are horrible I got you
up here safe and sound, didn't I?

231
00:12:53,780 --> 00:12:54,610
Nothing.

232
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:55,975
Not even a telescope.

233
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,200
How can that be?

234
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:59,420
Who do you suppose this is?

235
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:00,870
Huh?

236
00:13:01,020 --> 00:13:01,850
Whoa.

237
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:03,657
That's a mighty big painting.

238
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:05,387
Can you find a light switch?

239
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:06,530
Oh.

240
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:10,720
Did you turn on the
lights? No. Then who did?

241
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,640
Maybe the light's voice activated.

242
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:16,084
I've seen this portrait before.

243
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:17,817
In the dining hall, I think.

244
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:20,420
She must be very important to Pegasus.

245
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:24,057
But I haven't seen her at all
since we've been in the castle.

246
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:26,460
Do you think maybe she's Pegasus' wife?

247
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:29,540
Isn't it past your bedtimes?

248
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:31,730
Pegasus!

249
00:13:31,813 --> 00:13:32,900
How'd you find us?

250
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:36,860
A little birdie told me it saw
you three climbing up the walls.

251
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:38,877
Yeah, well, we're on to you, Pegsy.

252
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:39,790
Listen up.

253
00:13:39,873 --> 00:13:41,977
You've been spying on
Kybus cards from up here.

254
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:43,240
The jig is up.

255
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:45,027
Why don't you just admit it?

256
00:13:46,200 --> 00:13:47,030
Hmm.

257
